<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="030" project="spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI">
  <metadata>
    <title>Extend Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 with FIC creation (FR-C4)</title>
    <phase>3 Rollout</phase>
    <gate>020 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>auth tag; provisioning automation another project is blocked on; silent failure mode.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Scripted Azure CLI work with an exact recipe already proven by hand.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>E</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>020</deps>
    <tags>auth,infra,azure,scripts,cross-project</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add idempotent federated-identity-credential creation to the existing app-registration script. No FIC automation exists anywhere in the repo — the dev FIC was created by hand. SEQUENCE THIS EARLY: customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1 task 130 (Wave G-3) is soft-blocked on it.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with Azure CLI / Entra scripting experience.</role>
  <goal>Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 can create a FIC for a given (tenant, app registration, UAMI) idempotently, verified by performing an actual token exchange.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Verified exhaustively: zero repo automation creates a FIC, and even the existing GitHub Actions OIDC FIC was hand-run (.github/D-11:61, Application Administrator required). PROVISIONING-CHANGE-REQUEST §3.2 assigned this script as auth-v4's to own; their reply (AUTH-V4-CHANGE-REQUEST-RESPONSE) confirms task 130 will invoke it if it lands first, else build a duplicate that must then be reconciled. This is the one item outside the dev-only boundary.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">scripts/Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/PHASE-0-LIVE-VERIFICATION.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/PROVISIONING-CHANGE-REQUEST.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies><dependency task="020" status="pending">The provider defines what the FIC must satisfy</dependency></dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: issuer is the HOSTING tenant's /v2.0 OIDC endpoint; subject is the UAMI's principalId (object ID), NOT its clientId — that is the commonest silent error; audience is exactly api://AzureADTokenExchange.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: MUST retry on AADSTS70021 (propagation delay, minutes). Without it, onboarding fails intermittently in a way that looks like a permissions problem.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: MUST verify by PERFORMING A TOKEN EXCHANGE, not by checking that creation returned success. A misconfigured FIC creates cleanly and fails only at exchange.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: idempotent — re-running against an existing FIC is a no-op, not a duplicate or an error.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: extend the EXISTING script. Do not create a new one — provisioning expects to invoke this path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: scripts/ is a coordination overlap with customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1. Run /conflict-check before opening the PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Entra federated identity credentials, PowerShell provisioning</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/PHASE-0-LIVE-VERIFICATION.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/TENANCY-AND-CREDENTIALS.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/redis-cache-azure-setup.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read the existing script's idempotency and tenant-awareness conventions; match them.</step>
    <step>Add a FIC-creation function taking (tenantId, appRegistrationId, uamiPrincipalId, name).</step>
    <step>Add AADSTS70021 retry with backoff.</step>
    <step>Add exchange-based verification.</step>
    <step>Test against the dev app registration — the existing mi-bff-api-dev-assertion must be detected as already present and be a no-op.</step>
    <step>Notify customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1 that the extension has landed.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The Model 2 tenancy question raised in PROVISIONING-CHANGE-REQUEST §9.2 is still unanswered when parameterising for cross-tenant use — STOP. A cross-tenant FIC is structurally impossible and would create cleanly then fail silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="modify">scripts/Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/decisions/030-fic-automation.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Creating a FIC for a new (app-reg, UAMI) pair succeeds and is verified by an actual token exchange.</criterion>
    <criterion>Re-running against the existing dev FIC is a no-op, not an error or a duplicate.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: a FIC created with the UAMI's clientId instead of its principalId is DETECTED by the exchange verification, not reported as success.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: AADSTS70021 immediately after creation is retried, not surfaced as failure.</criterion>
    <criterion>The script's existing behaviour is unchanged when the new function is not invoked.</criterion>
    <criterion>/conflict-check run against customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1 before the PR.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
